#9. Search an Element in Binary Tree

We can use DFS recursively.
int search(struct Node *root, int key)
{
    if (root == NULL)
        return 0;

    if (root->data == key)
        return 1;

    if (search(root->left, key))
        return 1;

    return search(root->right, key);
}
Example:
       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \
   40 50
Search 50:
10 → 20 → 40 → 50
Output:
Found
