12. Mirror a Binary Tree
This is an important recursion problem.
Original:
       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \
   40 50
Mirror:
       10
      /  \
     30   20
         / \
        50 40
Code
void mirror(struct Node *root)
{
    if (root == NULL)
        return;

    struct Node *temp;

    temp = root->left;
    root->left = root->right;
    root->right = temp;

    mirror(root->left);
    mirror(root->right);
}
Logic
At every node:
Swap(left, right)
Then recursively mirror both subtrees.
